  (text "Pixel PCB (one per house). 12 V, WS2814F driver, 3 x RGBW 5050 LEDs, 3 per channel in series.\nChain in on J1 (male), out on J2 (female). Servo pinout: 1 = data, 2 = +12 V, 3 = GND.\nReversed plug: GND and data swap. This house's ground (and everything downstream) returns mostly\nthrough the upstream R3/DOUT (DOUT sink rated 10 mA min at 0.4 V). D1 clamps our DIN within the rails,\nand R2 limits the current through D1.\nOffset plug (one pin over): 12 V can land on DATA_IN. R2 limits the current into VDD through D1\n(~7 mA); VDD must stay under its 5.3 V absolute max.\nR4 moves ~2 V of the red channel's excess headroom off the WS2814 (red Vf 1.8-2.4 V x3).\nWS2814F data order is W,R,G,B (datasheet p.4); set the color order in WLED to match.\nFootprints for U1 and D2-D4 are in the project library village.pretty (see README).\nTBD: R2 value, R4 value. Fab-board tests: reversed plug\n(upstream DOUT / Dig-Quad output survive), offset plug (VDD <= 5.3 V)."
    (at 25.4 160.02 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
    (uuid "36047d4e-f36f-4a66-bb17-d7a448f881be")
  )
